  "narration": {
    "title": "The Bats Take Over: Alvarez and Schwarber Set the Pace",
    "intro": "Today the focus swings from the mound to the plate. Yordan Alvarez is quietly having the best season of any hitter in the game, and Kyle Schwarber is putting balls in the seats at a rate no one else can match. Here's who's swinging it best right now.",
    "offense_lead": "The Cubs top the team-OPS board at .768, a hair ahead of the Dodgers at .758. Washington, Milwaukee and Colorado fill out the five, so Chicago's lineup is the deepest going even without a single runaway name.",
    "bats_lead": "Yordan Alvarez leads the elite hitters at a 1.023 OPS, up a touch on the week and now 39 homers deep. Pete Crow-Armstrong sits second at .938 despite a slightly cool week, with James Wood and Shohei Ohtani holding steady behind him.",
    "season_leaders_lead": "Kyle Schwarber owns the home-run race at 45, with Crow-Armstrong (42) and Junior Caminero (41) chasing. On the batting side, Luis Arraez leads at .315, a nose ahead of Alvarez at .310, while Alec Burleson tops the RBI list at 111.",
    "hr_lead": "Randy Arozarena had the loudest power week, three homers to reach 25, two of them in back-to-back games against the Athletics. Caminero, Jake Bauers and Ben Rice each added a pair, keeping the top of the board crowded."
  }
